From: Nabu Linux contributors
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_smbx: correct SMB5 USB ADC units

ADC5_USB_IN_V_16 is already converted to input microvolts by the ADC
provider using the 1:16 prescale from DT. Multiplying it by 16 again makes
a 4.8 V USB input appear as 77 V.

ADC5_USB_IN_I returns the sense voltage in microvolts. PM8150B uses 0.2 V/A
in buck mode, so multiply by five to report microamps. The existing helper
only reads while charging, so this does not describe the boost-mode scale.

This corrects telemetry only; it does not change input limits or charging
policy. Leave SMB2 current conversion unchanged.

---
 drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c | 16 ++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c
@@ -679,16 +679,16 @@ static int smb_get_property(struct power_supply *psy,
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CURRENT_MAX:
 		return smb_get_current_limit(chip, &val->intval);
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CURRENT_NOW:
-		return smb_get_iio_chan(chip, chip->usb_in_i_chan,
+		ret = smb_get_iio_chan(chip, chip->usb_in_i_chan,
 					 &val->intval);
-	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_VOLTAGE_NOW:
-		ret = smb_get_iio_chan(chip, chip->usb_in_v_chan,
-					 &val->intval);
-		if (!ret) {
-			if (chip->gen == SMB5)
-				val->intval *= 16;
-		}
+		/* SMB5 buck-mode current sense is 0.2 V/A. */
+		if (!ret && chip->gen == SMB5)
+			val->intval *= 5;
 		return ret;
+	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_VOLTAGE_NOW:
+		/* The ADC provider has already applied the DT prescale. */
+		return smb_get_iio_chan(chip, chip->usb_in_v_chan,
+					 &val->intval);
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_ONLINE:
 		return smb_get_prop_usb_online(chip, &val->intval);
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_STATUS:
